{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Just load the wagon
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
My [C]grandpa had a sayin' that I got from him no [G]doubt
[G]One day he had me loadin' hay till I was plum wore [C]out
[C]I said, "If I load any more, this mule will be [F]zigzagging"
He [G]said, "Don't worry 'bout the mule, now, you just load the [C]wagon"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Don't you worry 'bout the mule, now, you just load the [G]wagon
[G]Pile it on till you can see them old springs [C]a-saggin'
[C]I ain't seen a load we couldn't pull and I ain't [F]braggin'
[G]Don't you worry 'bout the mule, now, you just load the [C]wagon
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
I married me a country girl and I knew I'd found a winner
I told her to fix a couple chickens and a ham for dinner
She said, "If you eat all that stuff you'll bend over gaggin'"
I said, "Don't worry 'bout the mule, now, you just load the wagon"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
She asked if I want children, I said, "Eight or ten"
"But then we'd better soon get started," she said with a grin
"But feeding all that bunch is gonna keep your butt a-draggin'"
I said, "Don't worry 'bout the mule, now, you just load the wagon"
{end_of_chorus}
